#string STR_PM_LITTLE_TITLE #language en-US "LITTLE CPU cluster"
#string STR_PM_LITTLE_MODE #language en-US "LITTLE policy"
#string STR_PM_LITTLE_NATIVE #language en-US "Native (keep board policy)"
#string STR_PM_LITTLE_CUSTOM #language en-US "Custom maximum frequency"
#string STR_PM_LITTLE_HELP #language en-US "Native leaves the LITTLE OPP table, boot point and voltage policy unchanged. Custom requests one additional top OPP above the native maximum while preserving all native entries and the boot point. The complete CPU profile is rejected if any request cannot be supported."
#string STR_PM_LITTLE_FREQ #language en-US "LITTLE maximum frequency (MHz)"
#string STR_PM_LITTLE_FREQ_HELP #language en-US "1800-2400 MHz in 10 MHz steps. 2400 MHz is an experimental software ceiling, not a hardware rating or stability guarantee. A request below the native maximum is rejected. A request equal to it retains the native table and cannot raise its voltage floor."
#string STR_PM_LITTLE_VOLT #language en-US "LITTLE top OPP minimum voltage (mV)"
#string STR_PM_LITTLE_AUTO_VOLT #language en-US "Native top OPP voltage (0)"
#string STR_PM_LITTLE_VOLT_HELP #language en-US "0 retains the native top OPP voltage floor; 550-950 mV requests a minimum for an added top OPP. PM retains at least the native floor and applies the board margin and coupling checks. Fixed LITTLE supplies are never changed; a request above their configured native voltage is rejected. Native mode ignores this setting."
